are further very careful to avoid any peroxidation, applying generous
doses of lipid antioxidants, and constantly refrigerating them and
otherwise keeping them out of heat, light, and oxygen.  And of course,
McDonald's oils aren't kept frying around all day, getting peroxidized
with the constant heat and recycled use (such as in the case of their
fries).  And no, the smell from McDonalds and other fast food joints.
This has nothing to do with the fact that using fresh, clean
